course: dictionary
lesson: 849
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one is meant. The word beta is a good example. «Alphabet» comes from alpha and beta, the first two letters of the Greek alphabet, so here beta is a letter.
explain: «Priya's grandma in Leicester smiles: "Pyjamas, shampoo and bungalow are Hindi words, beta!"» Here beta is not a letter. It is a loving word for a child, used in Hindi and Urdu, and the smile tells you it is kind.
explain: In computing, a beta version is an early version of a game, app or program that users test before the final one. Science uses beta as a name too, as in beta rays and beta-carotene. Always check the clues: is it a letter, a name, or a loving word?
explain: Online, some people use beta as an insult for a weak or shy person. This is unkind, so do not use it that way. Context helps you spot it, and you should never use it to hurt someone.
fact: Beta (β) is the second letter of the Greek alphabet, after alpha.
fact: A beta version of a game, app or program is an early version that users test before the final one.
fact: In science, beta names things such as beta rays, a kind of radiation.
fact: Beta-carotene is the orange colour in carrots; the body turns it into vitamin A, which is needed for the eyes.
fact: Online, beta is a slang insult for a weak or shy person; it is unkind.
exercise: «Alphabet» comes from alpha and beta. In this word, what is beta? | A colour in carrots | *A letter, the second in the Greek alphabet | A shy person | A kind of game
exercise: «Priya's grandma in Leicester smiles: "Pyjamas, shampoo and bungalow are Hindi words, beta!"» What does beta mean here? | A letter of the Greek alphabet | A test that finds bugs in a program | *A loving word for a child | A type of radiation
exercise: What is a beta version of a game? | A game with no sound | The final version sold in shops | A game only for grown-ups | *An early version that users test before the final one
test: Which name is a kind of radiation in science? | *Beta rays | Beta version | Alphabet | Beta-carotene
test: «Carrots are orange because of beta-carotene, which the body turns into vitamin A.» What is beta-carotene? | A loving word for a child | *The orange colour in carrots | The second letter of the alphabet | A kind of game
exam: In «the beta version of the app crashed», what does beta mean? | The second letter of the Greek alphabet | A weak or shy person | *An early version being tested by users | A kind of radiation
